{
 "id": "GtaCheatCodesC02",
 "slug": "gta-cheat-codes/c02",
 "chapter": "The rules",
 "topic": "What if GTA6 cheat codes worked in real life?",
 "script": [
  {
   "beat": "p1",
   "text": "It starts on a Saturday. The controller doesn't plug into anything. It doesn't even have batteries."
  },
  {
   "beat": "p2",
   "text": "But when you press the first code on the list, just to see, something chimes. And right in front of your face, in glowing letters only you can see: Cheat activated. Invincible."
  },
  {
   "beat": "p3",
   "text": "You poke your arm with a fork. Nothing. You drop a dictionary on your foot. Nothing. Not even a red mark. You throw yourself down all fourteen stairs, on purpose. It doesn't even tickle."
  },
  {
   "beat": "p4",
   "text": "The rules are on the back of the list, in tiny, old handwriting."
  },
  {
   "beat": "p5",
   "text": "One. A cheat stays on until you enter the same code again."
  },
  {
   "beat": "p6",
   "text": "Two. Nobody else can see the letters."
  },
  {
   "beat": "p7",
   "text": "And three. Never, ever enter the last code."
  },
  {
   "beat": "p8",
   "text": "Under all the scribbles, there's one word. You can't quite read it. Not yet."
  }
 ],
